 date="2026-10-02T17:30:10Z"
 content="""
> Now that you are saying this, is a new option even necessary?
> --test-readonly already takes a filename that is expected to be present
> on the remote, so instead of adding a new option --test-readonly could
> ensure that this key can't be removed, and that a different key can't be
> stored (and that removeKey succeeds on this not-present key).

I think it needs a new option. Someone might be using --test-readonly with
a file that they don't want to lose. Currently it never tries to remove a
file from a readonly remote, so that is safe enough, though not really
documented as such.
"""]]
